# ---------------- Barracks.events (Task 27 Part F example) ----------------
# The production building from Tasks 18 D and 27 D: it trains units and researches upgrades,
# then shows both on a command card with `bind`.
#
# WHAT IT SHOWS
#   · `train Marine` queues production through ProductionManager (cost/affordance held by the
#     `can afford` gate, exactly as the building sheets do)
#   · a finished Marine is spawned beside the building, so training ends with a unit on the map
#     (`when Barracks finishes training Marine` -> `spawn Marine at me offset 120`); the scene
#     needs an actor called `Marine` to stage the clones, even a hidden one
#   · the card's Train button doubles as the readout: `my queue count` is how many Marines are
#     still queued and `my train left` how many whole seconds the active one has left
#   · `research "Stim Pack"` queues the upgrade from Upgrades.events, charging the owner's bank
#   · `when research finishes` fires once when the level lands (`Player1 StimPack`)
#   · `bind progress of ResearchBar to my ResearchProgress` paints the bar from the 0-100 value
#     ResearchManager writes on this building while it works, and `ResearchName` labels it
#   · `lift off` / `land` (Task 28 Part E): the building rises to `my LiftHeight`, its queues
#     pause and its build-grid cell frees while it is up, then it lands and the work resumes
#
# HOTKEYS ARE SELECTION-SCOPED (Task 29 Part E): `when W is pressed` fires on every sheet in the
# scene, so each block starts with `me is selected`. Without that gate a key pressed anywhere
# would train, research or lift a building the player was not even looking at — the card's
# buttons were the only scoped route, and the hotkeys were global.
#
# SETUP (editor): an EventSheet on the building, Event File = `Barracks`. `ResearchBar` and
# `ResearchLabel` are optional UI actors; without them the binds simply do nothing. The Train
# readout binds to the card's `TrainMarineButton`, so it needs that button in the scene.
#
# `StimPackRequires` in Upgrades.events names `Barracks`, so researching it anywhere else is
# refused by the manager (with one warning) instead of silently working.
bind progress of ResearchBar to my ResearchProgress
bind ResearchLabel to my ResearchName
# The card's Train button is also this building's readout, so there is no second label to place:
# "Train Marine (W)  2 left, 4s" while it works and "0 left, 0s" when the queue is empty.
bind TrainMarineButton to my queue count and my train left format "Train Marine (W)  {0} left, {1}s"

when me appears
  set my MaxHealth to 1000
  set my Health to 1000
  set my unit type to "land"
  # A building dropped into a scene by hand was never placed by the build registry, so it has no
  # building state for the card to read (Task 29 Part E). This one line is what makes
  # `selection is all buildings`, the building command card and the right-click rally see it.
  set my Building to 1
  # How high this building rises. `lift off` reads it before `LiftOffHeight` or the 200 default,
  # so the L key and the card's Lift button cannot lift it to two different heights.
  set my LiftHeight to 20

# ---- selection feedback ---------------------------------------------------------------
when me is selected
  print "Barracks selected"

when me is deselected
  print "Barracks deselected"

# ---- train a Marine (W): one order per press, gated on the unit's cost variables ---------
# The `unless my Altitude ...` line is the flying gate from Task 28 Part C — no training while
# the building is up in the air. It reads the altitude rather than `me is airborne` so a
# building standing on its own ground needs no ground probe.
when W is pressed
  me is selected
  unless my Altitude is higher than 0
  can afford Marine
  train Marine

# ---- research Stim Pack (R): the upgrade table prices it -------------------------------
# The price comes from Upgrades.events (`StimPackCost`), so the manager checks the bank and
# refuses with one warning when it is short — a `can afford` gate would read only live globals.
when R is pressed
  me is selected
  research "Stim Pack"

# The level is already applied (`Player1 StimPack` is 1) before this event runs, so a
# `when Player1 StimPack changes` sheet sees the new number on the same tick.
when research finishes
  play sound "research_complete"

when production queue is empty
  print "Barracks: idle"

# ---- the finished unit walks out of the building ---------------------------------------
# Production itself only empties the queue; something has to put the unit on the map, which is
# this sheet's job (the engine has no unit table to spawn from). The offset puts it at the
# building's door instead of inside its model, and the clone keeps this scene's `Marine` sheet.
when Barracks starts producing Marine
  print "Barracks: training Marine"

when Barracks finishes training Marine
  spawn Marine at me offset 120
  print "Barracks: Marine ready"

# ---- lift off / land (L / K): the flying barracks from Task 28 Part E ---------------------
# Both keys are selection-scoped like the training hotkeys. `lift off` rises to `my LiftHeight`
# (20) and, without one, to `LiftOffHeight` or 200; `land` needs none: it puts the building down
# on the ground under it.
when L is pressed
  me is selected
  lift off

when K is pressed
  me is selected
  land

when me lifts off
  print "Barracks: airborne"

when me lands
  print "Barracks: down"
